## Additional Insights\n* Imagine you are trying to teach a **blindfolded robot** how to sort colorful LEGO bricks into different bins.\n\nThe robot has no idea what colors are, so at first, it just grabs bricks and tosses them randomly into bins.\n* Most of the time, the blue brick ends up in the yellow bin, and the red brick ends up in the green bin.\n* It’s a total mess!\n\nHere is how the robot learns, step-by-step:\n\n### 1.\n* The "Oops!" Moment (The Error)\nEvery time the robot drops a brick into the wrong bin, you stand there with a whistle.'}
